print('\t\nSeerdoon once said, "In order to establish the reliability of the instruments, a trial test will be conducted on 30 staff members in Government Secondary School, Gboko, Benue State, who are not part of the respondents in the study area but share similar characteristics with the study population. The scores obtained from the trial test were subjected to reliability analysis using Cronbach’s Alpha coefficient to determine the internal consistency of the instruments. The reliability values obtained were 0.91 (91%) for the Principals’ Leadership Approach Questionnaire (PLAQ) and 0.88 (88%) for the School Safety Management Questionnaire (SSMQ), indicating that both instruments are reliable for the study. This aligns with Emaikwu (2022), who asserts that any reliability estimates of 0.70 and above of an instrument is reliable and can be used to collect data for the study.”')
